/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 34 0 R
/E (Loyola College \(Autonomous\), Chennai, established in 1925 by the Society of Jesus \(Jesuits\), is one of India's premier institutions of higher education. Affiliated with the University of Madras and granted autonomous status in 1978, the college is renowned for its academic excellence, research, innovation, and commitment to social responsibility. Spread across a lush 79.5-acre campus in the heart of Chennai, Loyola offers a vibrant learning environment with diverse undergraduate, postgraduate, and doctoral programmes. Guided by its motto, "Let Your Light Shine," the institution fosters holistic education, global perspectives, ethical leadership, and sustainable development, making it a distinguished destination for scholars and learners worldwide. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [66]
>>
endobj
