287 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 34 0 R
/E (The PG and Research Department of Advanced Zoology & Biotechnology, Loyola College \(Autonomous\), Chennai, is one of the premier life science departments in India with a rich legacy of academic excellence and research. Originating from the Department of Natural Sciences established in 1948, it evolved into a full-fledged Department of Zoology in 1957 and was recognized as a Research Centre by the University of Madras in 1965. The department currently offers B.Sc. in Advanced Zoology & Biotechnology, M.Sc. in Zoology, and Ph.D. programmes, fostering innovation in animal sciences, biotechnology, ecology, molecular biology, environmental monitoring, and biodiversity conservation. Equipped with modern laboratories, an internationally recognized zoology museum, and a strong culture of interdisciplinary research, the department is committed to advancing scientific knowledge while promoting sustainable development and global academic collaboration. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [69]
>>
endobj
